From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] main: include fcntl.h for open() and O_RDONLY

is_input_device() calls open(path, O_RDONLY), but main.c includes no
<fcntl.h>. It compiles for FuriLabs because something in their include
chain happens to pull it in; with OE's GCC 15, which defaults to C23
where an implicit declaration is an error rather than a warning, it
fails:

  main.c:765:10: error: implicit declaration of function 'open';
                 did you mean 'popen'?
  main.c:765:21: error: 'O_RDONLY' undeclared (first use in this function);
                 did you mean 'MS_RDONLY'?

The second message is the giveaway that this is a missing include and
not a toolchain quirk: <sys/mount.h> is included and does define
MS_RDONLY, so the header that should have defined O_RDONLY is simply
absent.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <pthread.h>
 #include <dirent.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
 
 #include <sys/reboot.h>
 #include <sys/mount.h>
